#: ../../../../../../docs/reference/platforms/support.md:108
msgid ""
"从完整源码根执行。查询给出可选事实和模式，不能代替全装配准入或运行结果。Native需要显式test support，物理MCU保持 "
"`not_executed`，精确边界见[验证参考](qualification.md)。"
msgstr ""
"Run from the complete source root. Queries describe available facts and "
"modes; they do not replace admission of the complete assembly or execution "
"results. Native requires explicit test support; physical MCU status remains "
"`not_executed`. See [validation reference](qualification.md) for exact "
"boundaries."

msgid ""
"TFBGA216、2 MiB Flash、320 KiB 主 SRAM、64 KiB CPU-only CCM；显式 HSI168 "
"RUN，并保留 direct HSI16；按精确模式开放 FMC／SAI／LTDC／DMA2D／QuadSPI，PLLSAI 共享 M。GPIO"
" 软件参考仅开放 PJ0／PK3 的 input／output、baremetal，不推广到其它 J／K pad 或 PCB。普通 Flash "
"写擦覆盖两个物理 bank，OPTCR1 维护不受支持"
msgstr ""
"TFBGA216, 2 MiB Flash, 320 KiB main SRAM, 64 KiB CPU-only CCM; explicit "
"HSI168 RUN with direct HSI16 retained; FMC/SAI/LTDC/DMA2D/QuadSPI are "
"enabled by exact mode, and PLLSAI shares M. The GPIO software reference "
"enables only PJ0/PK3 input/output on baremetal, without extending to "
"other J/K pads or PCBs. Ordinary Flash programming and erase cover both "
"physical banks; OPTCR1 maintenance is unsupported"

msgid ""
"按精确器件和已审路线选择 GPIO input／output、四档显式输出速度与 EXTI0–15；PVD 原始电平／事件。F479NI 的 "
"J／K 当前只提供上表两条 GPIO 软件路线，不授予 EXTI。EXTI 的 `hardware-event` 只产生 EMR "
"硬件事件，不取得 IRQ 或软件队列。省略速度保留已有配置，PC13–15 输出限制为 LOW；晶振 LSE 占用时 PC13 "
"保持静默，晶振和调试引脚仍受资源约束。单 pin 可显式声明 `active_high`，生成复用授权 port 的只读逻辑 "
"signal；省略时无 signal，不从初始电平推导极性。软件事件保留 COALESCED／LOSS，不提供自动消抖、精确边沿时间或 BOR "
"资格"
msgstr ""
"GPIO input/output, four explicit output speeds and EXTI0–15 are selected"
" by exact device and reviewed route, with raw PVD levels/events. F479NI "
"J/K currently provides only the two GPIO software routes above, without "
"EXTI admission. EXTI `hardware-event` produces only EMR hardware events,"
" acquiring no IRQ or software queue. Omitting speed preserves existing "
"configuration; PC13–15 output speed is limited to LOW. PC13 remains "
"quiet when the LSE crystal owns its pads; oscillator and debug pins "
"retain resource constraints. A single pin may explicitly declare "
"`active_high`, generating a readonly logical signal that reuses its "
"authorized port. Omitting it generates no signal; polarity is not "
"inferred from the initial level. Software events retain COALESCED/LOSS; "
"no automatic debounce, precise edge timing or BOR qualification is "
"supplied."
